{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfeVfk4wLfh4YedpNkcJU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the rejected candidate with a different mechanism, and it passes the self-check with `OK`. The smoke fit's ELPD-LOO was −1358.9, compared with −1380.4 for the current best model, `local_representativeness`. That smoke fit was a single 100-draw chain, so the number is only indicative, and the check did not test novelty, convergence or fit time.\n\n**Why the first attempt failed:** it gave each person their own ideal switch rate, which made it an exact duplicate of `personal_alternation_ideal` (RMSE 0.00000 on the novelty pool). Four person-specific alternation models are already in the set, so I dropped that idea instead of adjusting it.\n\n**New model: `position_weighted_switch_impression`.** It follows the brief's push toward information the current models ignore, which here is *where* in the sequence the switches happen:\n- People judge how often the coin switches mainly from one end of the sequence. A fitted parameter `gamma` sets the direction and strength: above 0 they focus on the last flips, below 0 on the first.\n- They compare that position-weighted switch rate with an ideal rate shared by everyone (`rho`). The closer a sequence is, the more random it looks; `beta` sets how strongly that drives the choice.\n- So two sequences with the same number of switches can be judged differently, depending on whether the switches or the repeats sit at the end people attend to.\n- It has three parameters and no per-person ones.\n\nIt doesn't directly target the critique's strongest result, which is that people differ in how much they like alternation. That gap is already covered by the person-specific models.\n\n**Remaining risk:** if the fit lands on `gamma` ≈ 0 (no positional weighting), the model reduces to a plain shared-ideal alternation model. It might then predict too much like an existing model and be rejected as a near-duplicate again, and since this was the repair attempt, that rejection would be final.\n\nAll three files are in `iter_0/candidate_2_repair_1/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3116,"cache_read_input_tokens":48375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3116,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":658,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"485a5c20-a53d-40bf-a1a2-e0897c27a5e8","uuid":"5986b8aa-85f7-4fe0-8825-75261fcc6da3","timestamp":"2026-10-03T02:13:28.820Z","request_id":"req_011CfeVfj5uW62BLbVk7E84t"}
